## THE MODE — read this twice

**CODE_PATCH.** This service runs **VITEST** (`vi`, not `jest`). Your diff contains EXACTLY TWO files:
1. `services/api-gateway/src/routes/system-status.ts` — TWO hunks: one changed line, then one inserted block.
2. `services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1248-n-1-system-status-troubleshooting-marks.test.ts` — ONE NEW file.
**Nothing else.** Write the paths as `services/api-gateway/...` — NEVER `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/...`.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

`generateTroubleshooting` (`:520-594`) builds the `troubleshooting` list that `GET /system/status` returns (`:480`). Its first branch (`:526-544`) takes every REQUIRED service whose status is not `'healthy'` and emits a `critical` item whose commands include `docker restart secuura-<name>` and `az containerapp revision restart …`. Since #1037 (KS-1101), `checkServiceHealth` (`:336-338`) reports a service that answers 200 `{status: 'degraded'}` as `'degraded'`, so a DEGRADED required service now falls into that branch: it is labelled critical and the operator is told to restart it. Degraded means the service is up and serving with a sick dependency; restarting it can turn a partial outage into a full one. **This task (the ticket's own "What to do"): give `degraded` its own branch — a `warning` that says to read what the service reports and fix that dependency, with NO restart command — and keep `critical` + restart for a service that is actually down.**

## WHY THE TEST CALLS THE CODE DIRECTLY

The cell does not boot the gateway. It mounts the `system-status` router ALONE in a bare express app, exactly as the existing `ks864a-dead-estate-helper.test.ts` does, with the global `fetch` stubbed so each probed host answers what the cell says. No `index.ts`, no middleware, no auth, no network: the request goes straight into the `/status` handler (`:394`), which calls `checkServiceHealth` and `generateTroubleshooting` in-process.

